AITrain Studio uses a harness-first development workflow.

At the beginning of every new task, automatically read:

- HARNESS.md
- docs/harness/current-status.md
- docs/harness/project-context.md
- docs/harness/implementation-checklist.md
- docs/harness/quality-gates.md

For UI work, also read:

- docs/harness/ui-guidelines.md

For large implementation work, also inspect:

- docs/product-roadmap-local-training-platform.md

docs/archive/AITrainStudio_后续实施方案.md is historical background only. Do not use it as the current phase status, next-step plan, or acceptance source unless the user explicitly asks for historical context.

Rules:

- Keep changes scoped.
- Preserve the Qt Widgets workbench architecture.
- Do not put long-running work in the GUI thread.
- Do not put training logic in MainWindow.
- Route long tasks through aitrain_worker.
- Use ProjectRepository for SQLite.
- Use plugin interfaces for model/dataset/export/inference behavior.
- Keep Qt 5.12+ compatibility unless explicitly changed.
- Use QStringLiteral for UI text.
- Avoid Chinese mojibake.
- Treat repository text as UTF-8; in Windows PowerShell use explicit UTF-8 reads such as `Get-Content -Encoding UTF8`.
- Use `git -c core.quotepath=false ...` when listing paths that may contain Chinese filenames.
- Production training is official-backend only: Ultralytics YOLO detection/segmentation and PaddleOCR Det/Rec official adapters.
- Do not represent removed diagnostic paths (`tiny_linear_detector`, shipped `python_mock`, small PaddleOCR Rec CTC, C++ segmentation/OCR scaffold training) as product backends.
- Do not claim customer-domain OCR readiness, clean Windows acceptance, package-root TensorRT reruns, unsupported-hardware TensorRT success, or new algorithm support without returned evidence.

Before finalizing code changes, run:

.\tools\harness-check.ps1

For encoding-only checks, run:

.\tools\encoding-check.ps1
